      "parameters": {
        "width": 1264,
        "height": 1504,
        "content": "# UGC Ads Factory — Automated AI Video Pipeline\nAn n8n workflow that takes a script and character description from a Google Sheet and produces a finished, stitched UGC-style video ad with no manual intervention.\n---\n\n## Overview\nThis workflow automates the full lifecycle of UGC video ad creation:\n\n1. **Image Generation** — An AI agent crafts a photorealistic selfie prompt from the character description. The image is generated via Kie API (Nano Banana Pro), uploaded to Google Drive, and shared.\n2. **Scene Scripting** — The generated image is analyzed by GPT-4o-mini for visual details. Claude Opus then splits the user's script into structured 8-second scenes with consistent visuals and environment-aware motion instructions.\n3. **Video Clip Generation** — Each scene is sent to Kie VEO3 API for video generation. Clips are polled until complete, then uploaded to Google Drive.\n4. **Video Stitching** — Once all scene clips are done, they are merged into a single final video using fal.ai FFmpeg. The result is uploaded to Drive and the sheet is updated with the final link.\n\n---\n\n## Google Sheets Structure\nThe workflow uses two tabs in a single spreadsheet:\n\n- **Videos** — The main input/output tab. Each row contains a script, character description, aspect ratio, and status. The workflow reads rows marked \"Create\" and updates them through \"Processing\" to \"Completed\" or \"Failed\", writing back the final video links.\n- **Video Data** — Scene-level tracking. Each scene gets its own row with scene number, script JSON, image URL, individual clip links, and status. Used to track progress and support per-scene retries.\n\n---\n\n## Triggers\n- A **30-minute schedule** triggers the image generation and scene scripting pipeline.\n- A **15-minute schedule** picks up scenes marked \"Redo\" for video clip generation and retry.\n- The workflow can also be **triggered by another workflow**.\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n- All API calls retry on failure with a 5-second delay.\n- Failed image or video generations update the sheet with error details and a \"Failed\" status.\n- Individual scenes can be retried by setting their status to \"Redo\" in the Video Data tab.\n- Video stitching only runs after confirming all scenes have completed successfully.\n\n---\n\n## External Services\n- **Kie API** — Image generation (Nano Banana Pro) and video generation (VEO3)\n- **OpenRouter (Claude Opus)** — Prompt engineering and scene script generation\n- **OpenAI (GPT-4o-mini)** — Image analysis for visual consistency\n- **fal.ai** — FFmpeg-based video merging\n- **Google Drive** — Asset storage\n- **Google Sheets** — Input/output and status tracking\n\n---\n\n## Usage\n1. Add a row to the \"Videos\" sheet with script, character description, and aspect ratio.\n2. Set \"LAUNCH CREATION\" to \"Create\".\n3. The workflow picks it up on the next scheduled run and processes it end-to-end.\n4. The final video link appears in the sheet once complete.\n\nTo retry a failed scene, set its status to \"Redo\" in the \"Video Data\" tab.\n"
